From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fizban <35464167+Fiztba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:53:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve register calls and hoisted jump tables without
 fallback entries

An unresolved JALR promoted every instruction of its function to an
indirect fallback entry, although a register call returns to its link
address like JAL. The resume entry it already queues is all the caller
needs; the callee is found through the function table at run time.

A switch whose table LUI the compiler hoisted into a saved register,
with the low half formed into another register by ADDIU rt, rs, %lo,
never matched the table search. That shape is now accepted when it
names a table listed under [jump_tables], so unconfigured code behaves
as before.

KFIV with the kfiv-decomp function boundaries and jump tables: 634
fallback functions (103,858 entries) -> 0. With the Ghidra map:
1,352 (119,442) -> 150 (6,046).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_analyzer.cpp | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_analyzer.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_analyzer.cpp
index ed7578d..e8dc8a0 100644
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_analyzer.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_analyzer.cpp
@@ -194,7 +194,11 @@ namespace ps2recomp
             {
                 if (jrInst->function == SPECIAL_JALR)
                 {
+                    // A register call returns to its link address like JAL does. The
+                    // resume entry is all the caller needs, so an unknown call target
+                    // never promotes the caller's instructions to fallback entries.
                     queueResumeEntryTarget(jrInst->address + 8u);
+                    continue;
                 }
 
                 bool foundTable = false;
@@ -276,6 +280,45 @@ namespace ps2recomp
                             }
                         }
 
+                        if (!foundTableAddress && adduIndex != -1 && !m_configJumpTableTargetsByAddress.empty())
+                        {
+                            // The compiler may hoist the table's LUI into a saved register
+                            // far above the switch and form the low half into another
+                            // register (ADDIU rt, rs, %lo). Accept that shape only when it
+                            // names a configured table, so unconfigured code is unaffected.
+                            for (uint32_t reg : {tableBaseReg, indexReg})
+                            {
+                                for (int i = adduIndex - 1; i >= 0 && i >= adduIndex - 8; --i)
+                                {
+                                    const auto &lowInst = instructions[i];
+                                    if (lowInst.opcode != OPCODE_ADDIU || lowInst.rt != reg || lowInst.rs == reg)
+                                    {
+                                        continue;
+                                    }
+                                    for (int j = i - 1; j >= 0; --j)
+                                    {
+                                        const auto &highInst = instructions[j];
+                                        if (highInst.opcode == OPCODE_LUI && highInst.rt == lowInst.rs)
+                                        {
+                                            const uint32_t candidate = (highInst.immediate << 16) +
+                                                                       static_cast<uint32_t>(lowInst.simmediate);
+                                            if (m_configJumpTableTargetsByAddress.contains(candidate + lwOffset))
+                                            {
+                                                tableAddress = candidate;
+                                                foundTableAddress = true;
+                                            }
+                                            break;
+                                        }
+                                    }
+                                    break;
+                                }
+                                if (foundTableAddress)
+                                {
+                                    break;
+                                }
+                            }
+                        }
+
                         if (foundTableAddress)
                         {
                             tableAddress += lwOffset;
